# Bundled Material typography fonts

Raw variable-TTF bytes embedded into `frust-material` via `include_bytes!`
(`plugins/material/src/tokens/fonts.rs`) behind the crate's `bundled-fonts`
Cargo feature (default on, the `plugins/glyph/fonts/` and `plugins/shadcn/fonts/`
precedent). An app that sets `default-features = false` on its `frust-material`
dependency ships none of these bytes.

This crate bundles two typefaces to ship Material 3 typography out of the box:
**Roboto Flex** for display/heading/body text and **Roboto Mono** for monospace.
Both families are sourced from Google Fonts; Roboto Mono is unmodified, and
Roboto Flex is a `wght`-only static-axis instance of the upstream variable
font (see the Roboto Flex "Modification" record below).

Roboto Flex declares no Reserved Font Name (the copyright lines carry no "with
Reserved Font Name" clause), so the unmodified face ships under its original
name with the full OFL-1.1 license text vendored (`roboto-flex/OFL.txt`), as the
license's license-inclusion term requires.

Roboto Mono is licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
(OFL-1.1), the same license as Roboto Flex — verified directly from the
shipped font's own `name` table (nameID 13/14: "This Font Software is
licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1",
https://openfontlicense.org; nameID 0 copyright: "Copyright 2015 The Roboto
Mono Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/robotomono)"), and
corroborated by its Google Fonts source path living under `ofl/`
(`google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/robotomono` — Google Fonts partitions its repo
by license, and `ofl/` is the OFL-1.1 tree, not `apache/`). The full OFL-1.1
license text is vendored at `roboto-mono/OFL.txt`. The variable font format
carries no additional licensing terms beyond the copyright and license text
herein.

Both font bytes are pure data: they are only ever returned by
`frust_material::font_data()`. Registering them into a live `TextContext` is a
shell's job — `frust_material::install()` pushes them through the facade's
`register_app_fonts` pending-font queue for the running shell to drain.

