### Modification

The vendored `roboto-flex/RobotoFlex.ttf` is **not** the unmodified upstream
bytes: it is a `wght`-only static-axis instance of the upstream variable font,
produced with `scripts/fonts/instance_variable_font.py` (fontTools
`varLib.instancer`, fontTools 4.63.0). `crates/frust-text` only ever drives
`StyleProperty::FontWeight`/`FontStyle` on a shaped run (see
`plugins/material/src/tokens/fonts.rs`'s module doc) — no component anywhere
requests `opsz`, `wdth`, `GRAD`, `slnt`, or any of Roboto Flex's parametric
axes (`XOPQ`/`YOPQ`/`XTRA`/`YTUC`/`YTLC`/`YTAS`/`YTDE`/`YTFI`) — so every axis
but `wght` always rendered at its own default position anyway. Pinning those
twelve axes at their default values and keeping only `wght` variable drops
their `gvar` deltas with no visual change and no glyph dropped (all 896 glyphs
kept; no subsetting). The vendored OFL-1.1 license text (`roboto-flex/OFL.txt`)
ships unchanged, and this instance declares no Reserved Font Name, the same as
upstream.

- **Upstream SHA-256** (pre-instancing download, per Google Fonts as retrieved
  2026-08-19, 1,684,624 B): `2bd17942bba38048b2f86e00cdd6fb2242035c0b2c843d5979bb24f13d5512ef`
- **Instanced SHA-256** (the bytes actually vendored, 175,900 B):
  `446aa9ee34d3ce037bfeda0143b27353e71ef8e37dc9a87111c7a0e18ee40567`
- **Command**:
  `python3 scripts/fonts/instance_variable_font.py plugins/material/fonts/roboto-flex/RobotoFlex.ttf plugins/material/fonts/roboto-flex/RobotoFlex.ttf --keep wght`
- **Date**: 2026-09-17
- **Remaining axis**: `wght` (100–1000), default 400 — unchanged from upstream
- **Regenerate when**: the text stack starts driving another axis (`opsz`,
  `wdth`, `GRAD`, `slnt`, or any parametric axis) — re-download the upstream
  variable font (the vendored file is already instanced, so instancing it
  again would only narrow the axis set further) and re-run the command above
  with an additional `--keep <axis>` per axis that must stay variable.

